From a89ada90b67f2fdf41823eb94a340f7d146e4f9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 01:40:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] UWP: diagnose memory write watches; refresh GPU data if
 protection fails

Effects drawn from vertex data the game rewrites every frame were invisible
on Xbox. The GPU only re-uploads guest memory after a write watch (page
protection + vectored exception handler) reports a CPU write.

- Log VirtualProtectFromApp failures, the vectored exception handler install
  result, and how often memory write watches fire.
- If memory protection ever fails (or clear_memory_page_state is set),
  invalidate CPU-uploaded shared memory pages at the end of every frame so
  they're uploaded again.
- XMA unknown register writes are logged at debug level (they flooded the
  log, which is flushed on every line on UWP).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01T2Eqt3AmpbNRB9dC5uwqee
